A document has a title and a body.

class Document
  attr_reader :title, :body

  def initialize(title, body)
    @title = title
    @body = body
  end

  def word_count
    body.split.size
  end

  def to_s
    "#{title}: #{word_count} words"
  end
end

Now we make one with a short note: doc = Document.new("A short note", "write code the way you explain it")
and we count its words: words = doc.word_count
then we print the document and the count: puts doc
and then the count again: puts !-1
